    ("fusion_export_step", "Export the active design to STEP (needs the 3D view).",
     {"outputPath": "required str"}, {"format": "str", "fileSizeKB": "int"}, 300, None, True, {"outputPath": "C:/out/board.step"}),
    ("fusion_import_step", "Bring a STEP in as 3D geometry placed with the board (the standard's import_step): the design's 3D PCB is brought forward and the STEP is imported into it as a new component (an enclosure, a bracket, a mating part) at `at` mm and `rotation` degrees from the board origin, so fusion_bodies and fusion_height_check measure the board against it. A STEP that imports nothing leaves no component behind. into:'new' opens the STEP as its own new Fusion design instead (the earlier behaviour). Save the design afterwards to keep it.",
     {"filePath": "required str (the STEP on the Fusion machine)", "at": "[x, y, z] mm from the board origin, default [0, 0, 0]", "rotation": "[rx, ry, rz] degrees, default [0, 0, 0]", "name": "the component's name (default the file's stem)", "expectDocument": "the design's name", "into": "'board' (default) or 'new'"},
     {"success": "bool", "id": "the occurrence's path", "name": "str", "bodies": "int", "bboxMm": "[x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1]", "documentsOpened": "int (0 when placed with the board)"}, 300, None, True, {"filePath": "C:/mech/enclosure.step", "at": [0, 0, -3]}),

    # ── Catalog completion (2026-08-14): 14 verbs that were LIVE but undescribed, caught by
    # the verb suite's reverse drift check. An undescribed verb is invisible to ab's Verbs
